From 0fc910c11607f237f7abbb7fd57dfcd8066e7251 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:34:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Cut long char-server list lines instead of ending the client

server_list builds each line of the char-server list in text[0x40]: the
new-server prefix (msg 0x1e2) and the name, then, as a String, a colour
code, the busy message, "  ^000000", that text and the state message,
and copies the result back with strcpy_s(text, 0x40, ...). A line of 64
bytes or more, as with longer busy or state messages, makes strcpy_s
call the invalid-parameter handler, and the client sets none, so it
ends. The prefix was also written with sprintf, using the message as
the format.

The prefix and the name are now kept in a String as well, the name
bounded by its 20-byte field as before, and server_line copies the
finished line into text cut by whole characters (text_prefix_length with
g_codePage). The prefix is copied as text. Lines that fit are unchanged.

Validation: test_name_text now also runs server_list with a one-byte
busy message, a line of 93 bytes with a 40-byte busy message and a state
message, an 80-byte state message on its own, and a line whose 63-byte
limit falls inside a two-byte CP949 character, which is left out. It
links core/text_format.c and user32.lib. The test ends the client's way
on the previous code, at strcpy_s, and fails with a plain byte cut. 45
cases. Release build without warnings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaQB81YtRGLtH8zvfX7WTY
